    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_1dbb53ed",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "landmine_weight_mapping",
      "label": "The text 'when you step on a landmine but you do not weigh enough' is mapped onto the visual scene of the 'DANGER MINES' sign and surrounding area.",
      "description": "The textual element describes a hypothetical scenario involving a landmine, which is directly analogous to the visual element — the 'DANGER MINES' warning sign — that is present in the image. The sign visually represents the landmine hazard mentioned in the text, creating an analogical mapping where the text's concept (landmine) is instantiated by the visual sign. The humor arises from the absurdity of the text's premise (not triggering the mine due to insufficient weight) being juxtaposed with the literal warning sign, implying the visual scene is the setting for the described event.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
