      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the textual material describing a hypothetical scenario",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the text 'when you step on a landmine but you do not weigh enough' because the text uses the second-person pronoun 'you', directly addressing the viewer and inviting them to imagine themselves in the described situation. This creates an implicit identification where the user is the subject of the hypothetical event.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
